WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:02.087
<i>"From this time</i>
<i>until the end of time.</i>

2
00:00:02.088 --> 00:00:06.092
we are the free and independent
Kingdom of the North."

3
00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:08.122
You'll give the Starks
our reply. cousin?

4
00:00:08.147 --> 00:00:09.428
I will. Your Grace.

5
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:11.330
Did you see my brother when you
were the Starks' guest?

6
00:00:11.364 --> 00:00:13.426
I did.

7
00:00:13.451 --> 00:00:15.110
Tell him he's not
been forgotten.

8
00:00:15.535 --> 00:00:17.570
( Grunts )

9
00:00:17.604 --> 00:00:19.705
( Panting )

10
00:00:19.773 --> 00:00:21.574
I'll do it.

11
00:00:21.608 --> 00:00:23.276
Come. brothers.
We'll leave him to it.

12
00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.111
Be quick about it.

13
00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:27.280
- ( Grunts )
- ( Sword clangs )

14
00:00:27.315 --> 00:00:29.917
I've yielded Winterfell
to Prince Theon.

15
00:00:29.951 --> 00:00:32.019
All of you should do
as he commands.

16
00:00:32.053 --> 00:00:34.154
Betray me and you will
wish you hadn't.

17
00:00:34.188 --> 00:00:35.522
Man:
<i>All hail the king.</i>

18
00:00:35.556 --> 00:00:37.057
- ( Groans )
- ( Crowd murmuring )

19
00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:39.192
- Who threw that?
- ( Crowd shouting )

20
00:00:40.127 --> 00:00:42.595
Get back!

21
00:00:45.265 --> 00:00:46.699
( Whimpering )

22
00:00:48.335 --> 00:00:50.169
You're all right now. little bird.
You're all right.

23
00:00:50.204 --> 00:00:51.938
Your brothers desert you?

24
00:00:51.972 --> 00:00:54.573
- We'll stop here.
- Think they're out looking for you?

25
00:00:54.575 --> 00:00:55.875
Yes.

26
00:00:58.012 --> 00:00:59.146
( Grunts )

27
00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.381
What might this be?
Let's go.

28
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.784
Amory Lorch.
Now!

29
00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:06.853
A man will do
what must be done.

30
00:01:09.791 --> 00:01:11.425
<i>Guard!</i>

31
00:01:11.459 --> 00:01:13.861
I have something for you
from Prince Theon.

32
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.430
( Gurgles )

33
00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.169
When I came to this city.
I had nothing.

34
00:01:22.204 --> 00:01:25.105
Today I am the richest
man in Qarth

35
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.940
with no regrets.

36
00:01:29.177 --> 00:01:32.112
Where are they?
Where are my dragons?!

37
00:01:32.146 --> 00:01:34.180
( Screeching )

38
00:01:41.221 --> 00:01:43.388
<i>( Theme music playing )</i>

39
00:01:43.413 --> 00:01:47.413
<font color=#00FF00>* Game of Thrones 2x07 *</font>
<font color=#00FFFF>A Man Without Honor</font>
Original Air Date on May 13. 2012

40
00:01:47.438 --> 00:01:51.438
== sync. corrected by <font color="#00ff00">elderman</font> ==

41
00:01:51.463 --> 00:03:26.431
♪

42
00:03:43.894 --> 00:03:45.762
A cripple?

43
00:03:45.796 --> 00:03:48.665
You let a cripple escape?

44
00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.530
<i>The boy can't walk.</i>

45
00:03:51.535 --> 00:03:53.536
but somehow
he slipped past you?

46
00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:57.173
The giant must have took him.

47
00:03:57.207 --> 00:03:59.475
The giant?

48
00:04:00.778 --> 00:04:03.012
Hodor?

49
00:04:03.046 --> 00:04:05.648
Oh. well.
that's all right. then.

50
00:04:05.683 --> 00:04:09.151
You let a halfwit
escape with a cripple.

51
00:04:09.186 --> 00:04:11.086
And Rickon. too?
The little one?

52
00:04:11.121 --> 00:04:14.656
Gone along with
the wildling woman.

53
00:04:14.691 --> 00:04:17.259
the one you were fucking.

54
00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:28.135
( Grunting )

55
00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:31.172
<i>( Man groaning )</i>

56
00:04:31.206 --> 00:04:35.009
( Panting )

57
00:04:36.178 --> 00:04:40.481
Right. get the horses
and the hounds.

58
00:04:42.984 --> 00:04:45.152
- ( Dogs barking )
- Come on. find the scent.

59
00:04:49.992 --> 00:04:52.160
Come on. where they going?

60
00:05:01.003 --> 00:05:02.203
Halt!

61
00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:08.943
Enjoying your first hunt?

62
00:05:08.978 --> 00:05:12.179
So far. hunting seems very similar
to riding. My Lord.

63
00:05:12.214 --> 00:05:13.682
With hunting.
there's blood at the end.

64
00:05:13.707 --> 00:05:15.649
They're little boys.

65
00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.098
I was a little boy
when I was torn away from

66
00:05:17.123 --> 00:05:19.052
my home and brought here.

67
00:05:19.053 --> 00:05:20.653
So I kept my word.

68
00:05:20.688 --> 00:05:22.622
I never ran away.

69
00:05:22.656 --> 00:05:25.759
If I find them soon enough.
I won't hurt them.

70
00:05:27.028 --> 00:05:29.830
Well. I'll hurt them.
but I won't kill them.

71
00:05:29.864 --> 00:05:32.900
Those boys are of far more value
to you alive than dead.

72
00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.935
They have no value
to me missing.

73
00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.505
Robb will have sent a force
to retake Winterfell by now.

74
00:05:37.539 --> 00:05:40.742
Robb's in the Riverlands.
My sister's in Deepwood Motte.

75
00:05:40.776 --> 00:05:43.478
<i>She'll get here</i>
<i>long before they do.</i>

76
00:05:43.512 --> 00:05:46.162
And Ned Stark always
said 500 men could hold

77
00:05:46.187 --> 00:05:47.782
Winterfell against 10.000.

78
00:05:47.783 --> 00:05:50.718
- <i>( Dogs barking )</i>
- Man: <i>We have a scent!</i>

79
00:05:50.752 --> 00:05:53.353
The hounds have the scent.

80
00:05:53.388 --> 00:05:55.889
Come. Maester.
don't look so grim.

81
00:05:55.923 --> 00:05:58.691
It's all just a game.

82
00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:15.775
Osha: We should have
took more food.

83
00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.944
We couldn't risk
going to the kitchens.

84
00:06:17.979 --> 00:06:19.446
Those people all love you.

85
00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.881
They would have given
you whatever you needed.

86
00:06:20.915 --> 00:06:22.750
And if Theon found out.
he'd hang them.

87
00:06:22.784 --> 00:06:25.752
- The boy can't survive on walnuts.
- I'm fine.

88
00:06:27.321 --> 00:06:30.056
We've been walking
since before sunrise.

89
00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.525
- Even Hodor will tire.
- Hodor.

90
00:06:32.559 --> 00:06:35.528
- Even you. sweet giant.
- ( Chuckles ) Hodor.

91
00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:39.298
<i>( Children shouting )</i>

92
00:06:39.333 --> 00:06:41.334
Wait. I know that farm.

93
00:06:41.368 --> 00:06:44.169
<i>I sent those two</i>
<i>Winterfell orphans there.</i>

94
00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.138
Jack and Billy.

95
00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:47.906
They'll give us some food.

96
00:06:47.941 --> 00:06:49.007
We can't risk it.

97
00:06:49.042 --> 00:06:50.709
If Theon tracks us here.
he'll torture them

98
00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.711
until he finds out
where we are.

99
00:06:52.746 --> 00:06:55.147
Billy climbs a tree
better than anyone.

100
00:06:55.182 --> 00:06:56.915
You've never seen me
climb a tree. little man.

101
00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.451
<i>They'll be after us</i>
<i>with hounds.</i>

102
00:06:59.486 --> 00:07:01.053
<i>We got a good start on them.</i>

103
00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.522
but we can't outrun
hounds forever.

104
00:07:28.582 --> 00:07:31.651
Did you pull a knife
on me in the night?

105
00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:43.361
What's the matter?

106
00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:45.263
Can't be the first time
you pressed your bone

107
00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:46.898
against a woman's ass.

108
00:07:49.034 --> 00:07:50.868
Let's move.

109
00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:59.043
Oh. it is the first time.

110
00:07:59.978 --> 00:08:02.280
How old are you. boy?

111
00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:05.083
I'm a man of the Night's Watch.

112
00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:09.688
You're a boy who's
never been with a girl.

113
00:08:13.393 --> 00:08:15.094
Don't your stones start to hurt

114
00:08:15.129 --> 00:08:17.697
if your bone never gets...

115
00:08:17.731 --> 00:08:19.832
Don't call them that.

116
00:08:19.867 --> 00:08:23.169
What. stones?

117
00:08:23.204 --> 00:08:24.871
Or bone?

118
00:08:24.905 --> 00:08:27.307
Neither.

119
00:08:27.341 --> 00:08:29.642
Both.

120
00:08:31.512 --> 00:08:33.212
Move!

121
00:08:38.285 --> 00:08:40.019
Ygritte: I heard they get
all swollen

122
00:08:40.054 --> 00:08:42.388
and bruised if you
don't use them.

123
00:08:42.423 --> 00:08:44.190
Of course. maybe that's
just what the lads say

124
00:08:44.224 --> 00:08:46.859
when they want me
feeling sorry for them.

125
00:08:46.894 --> 00:08:49.228
As if I'd feel sorry for them.

126
00:08:50.164 --> 00:08:52.832
Are there no girl crows?

127
00:08:54.167 --> 00:08:56.635
There are no women
of the Night's Watch. no.

128
00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.737
So the lads just do it
with each other?

129
00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:00.639
No.

130
00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:03.174
- Never?
- Never.

131
00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:05.777
We swore an oath.

132
00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:08.113
You have sheep at the Wall?

133
00:09:10.283 --> 00:09:12.317
With your hands. then?

134
00:09:12.352 --> 00:09:15.488
No wonder
you're all so miserable.

135
00:09:15.522 --> 00:09:16.990
Would you please shut up?

136
00:09:17.024 --> 00:09:19.159
( Mocking )
Would you please shut up?

137
00:09:20.261 --> 00:09:22.729
You think you're
better than me. crow.

138
00:09:22.763 --> 00:09:25.298
- I'm a free woman...
- You're a free woman?

139
00:09:25.332 --> 00:09:27.601
I might be your prisoner.
but I'm a free woman.

140
00:09:27.635 --> 00:09:29.569
If you're my prisoner.
you're not a free woman.

141
00:09:29.604 --> 00:09:31.204
That's what "prisoner" means.

142
00:09:31.239 --> 00:09:33.306
And you think you're free?

143
00:09:34.342 --> 00:09:36.309
You swore some stupid oath

144
00:09:36.344 --> 00:09:37.811
and now you can never
touch a girl.

145
00:09:37.845 --> 00:09:40.313
It was my choice
to say the words.

146
00:09:40.347 --> 00:09:42.215
- So you don't like girls?
- Of course I like girls.

147
00:09:42.249 --> 00:09:44.217
But you chose
never to touch them.

148
00:09:44.251 --> 00:09:46.954
That's the price you pay if you want
to be a man of the Night's Watch.

149
00:09:46.988 --> 00:09:48.822
So instead of getting
naked with a girl.

150
00:09:48.857 --> 00:09:50.391
you'd prefer
to invade our lands...

151
00:09:50.425 --> 00:09:52.092
Invade your lands?

152
00:09:52.127 --> 00:09:54.061
Wildlings raid
our lands all the time.

153
00:09:54.096 --> 00:09:56.998
Some of them tried to kill my
little brother. a crippled boy!

154
00:09:57.032 --> 00:09:59.001
They're not your lands!

155
00:09:59.035 --> 00:10:01.070
We've been here the whole time.

156
00:10:01.104 --> 00:10:02.995
You lot came along
and just put up a big wall

157
00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:04.674
and said it was yours.

158
00:10:04.675 --> 00:10:07.310
My father was Ned Stark.

159
00:10:07.345 --> 00:10:09.312
I have the blood
of the First Men.

160
00:10:09.346 --> 00:10:12.582
My ancestors lived here.
same as yours.

161
00:10:14.886 --> 00:10:17.020
So why are you fighting us?

162
00:10:33.039 --> 00:10:35.174
Go on.

163
00:10:40.114 --> 00:10:42.749
Now I want you
to tell me what happened.

164
00:10:42.783 --> 00:10:45.986
- Guard: <i>Come on. this way.</i>
- <i>( Man screaming )</i>

165
00:10:46.987 --> 00:10:49.622
<i>Come on. speak up.</i>
<i>Speak up.</i>

166
00:10:53.393 --> 00:10:54.860
( Sniffs )

167
00:10:54.894 --> 00:10:57.562
Wolfsbane...

168
00:10:57.596 --> 00:11:00.165
a rare substance.

169
00:11:00.199 --> 00:11:02.633
This is no common assassin.

170
00:11:02.668 --> 00:11:04.802
We hanged 20 men last night.

171
00:11:04.837 --> 00:11:07.638
I don't care if you hanged 100.

172
00:11:07.672 --> 00:11:09.173
A man tried to kill me.

173
00:11:09.207 --> 00:11:11.242
I want his name
and I want his head.

174
00:11:11.277 --> 00:11:12.744
Mountain: <i>We think it was</i>
<i>an infiltrator</i>

175
00:11:12.778 --> 00:11:15.614
from the Brotherhood
Without Banners.

176
00:11:15.648 --> 00:11:18.417
Pretentious name
for a band of outlaws.

177
00:11:18.451 --> 00:11:21.019
We can't allow rebels
behind our lines

178
00:11:21.054 --> 00:11:23.122
to harass us with impunity.

179
00:11:23.156 --> 00:11:25.257
We look like fools
and they look like heroes.

180
00:11:25.292 --> 00:11:27.025
<i>That's how kings fall.</i>

181
00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:29.228
I want them dead. every one.

182
00:11:29.262 --> 00:11:31.029
Killing them isn't the problem.

183
00:11:31.064 --> 00:11:32.999
<i>It's finding them.</i>

184
00:11:33.033 --> 00:11:35.301
Have you gone soft. Clegane?

185
00:11:35.335 --> 00:11:37.436
I always thought you had
a talent for violence.

186
00:11:37.471 --> 00:11:41.073
Burn the villages.
burn the farms.

187
00:11:41.108 --> 00:11:43.476
Let them know what it means
to choose the wrong side.

188
00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:44.944
Mmm.

189
00:11:47.514 --> 00:11:49.649
Is that mutton?

190
00:11:49.683 --> 00:11:51.184
Yes. My Lord.

191
00:11:51.218 --> 00:11:52.786
Don't like mutton.

192
00:11:53.787 --> 00:11:55.755
I'll bring something else.

193
00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.891
Leave it.

194
00:11:59.126 --> 00:12:01.427
- Are you hungry?
- No.

195
00:12:01.461 --> 00:12:03.095
Of course you are.

196
00:12:03.129 --> 00:12:04.663
Eat.

197
00:12:04.698 --> 00:12:07.933
I'll eat in the kitchen later.

198
00:12:07.968 --> 00:12:12.137
It's bad manners
to refuse a Lord's offer.

199
00:12:12.171 --> 00:12:14.273
Sit.

200
00:12:15.341 --> 00:12:16.842
Eat.

201
00:12:20.012 --> 00:12:21.379
You're small for your age.

202
00:12:22.848 --> 00:12:25.016
I suppose you've been
underfed your whole life.

203
00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.751
I eat a lot.

204
00:12:26.786 --> 00:12:29.955
- <i>I just don't grow.</i>
- Hmm.

205
00:12:33.259 --> 00:12:37.163
This will be my last war.

206
00:12:37.197 --> 00:12:39.332
win or lose.

207
00:12:40.401 --> 00:12:42.436
Have you ever lost before?

208
00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:45.473
Do you think I'd be in my position
if I had lost a war?

209
00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:56.151
But this is the one
I'll be remembered for.

210
00:12:56.185 --> 00:12:58.821
<i>The "War of Five Kings"</i>
<i>they're calling it.</i>

211
00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:03.393
My legacy will be determined
in the coming months.

212
00:13:05.229 --> 00:13:07.831
Do you know what legacy means?

213
00:13:09.834 --> 00:13:12.402
It's what you pass down
to your children

214
00:13:12.436 --> 00:13:15.805
and your children's children.

215
00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:18.875
It's what remains of you
when you're gone.

216
00:13:22.614 --> 00:13:25.782
Harren the Black thought this castle
would be his legacy.

217
00:13:27.385 --> 00:13:30.153
The greatest fortress
ever built...

218
00:13:30.188 --> 00:13:33.723
the tallest towers.
the strongest walls.

219
00:13:33.758 --> 00:13:37.294
The Great Hall had 35 hearths.

220
00:13:37.328 --> 00:13:40.464
35. Can you imagine?

221
00:13:40.498 --> 00:13:42.132
Look at it now...

222
00:13:43.334 --> 00:13:45.135
<i>a blasted ruin.</i>

223
00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:48.238
Do you know what happened?

224
00:13:48.272 --> 00:13:50.573
Dragons?

225
00:13:50.608 --> 00:13:54.678
Yes. dragons happened.

226
00:13:57.115 --> 00:14:01.618
Harrenhal was built to withstand
an attack from the land.

227
00:14:03.988 --> 00:14:06.889
A million men could have marched
on these walls

228
00:14:06.924 --> 00:14:09.292
and a million men
would have been repelled.

229
00:14:09.326 --> 00:14:14.930
But an attack from the air
with dragon fire... mm.

230
00:14:14.964 --> 00:14:18.366
Harren and all his sons
roasted alive within these walls.

231
00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:23.337
Aegon Targaryen
changed the rules.

232
00:14:23.371 --> 00:14:26.339
That's why every child alive
still knows his name

233
00:14:26.374 --> 00:14:28.475
300 years after his death.

234
00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.878
Aegon and his sisters.

235
00:14:32.013 --> 00:14:33.480
Mm?

236
00:14:33.515 --> 00:14:36.750
It wasn't just Aegon
riding his dragon.

237
00:14:36.784 --> 00:14:38.619
It was Rhaenys
and Visenya. too.

238
00:14:38.653 --> 00:14:40.922
Correct.

239
00:14:40.956 --> 00:14:43.191
A student of history. are you?

240
00:14:43.225 --> 00:14:45.694
Rhaenys rode Meraxes.

241
00:14:45.728 --> 00:14:47.563
Visenya rode Vhagar.

242
00:14:49.299 --> 00:14:51.867
I'm sure I knew that
when I was a boy.

243
00:14:51.902 --> 00:14:56.206
Visenya Targaryen
was a great warrior.

244
00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.142
She had a Valyrian steel sword
she called Dark Sister.

245
00:14:59.177 --> 00:15:01.478
Hmm.

246
00:15:01.513 --> 00:15:03.681
She's a heroine
of yours. I take it?

247
00:15:04.949 --> 00:15:06.583
Aren't most girls
more interested

248
00:15:06.618 --> 00:15:08.552
in the pretty maidens
from the songs?

249
00:15:08.586 --> 00:15:10.686
<i>Jonquil with the flowers</i>
<i>in her hair?</i>

250
00:15:10.721 --> 00:15:13.189
- Most girls are idiots.
- <i>Ha!</i>

251
00:15:14.558 --> 00:15:17.058
You remind me of my daughter.

252
00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.661
Where did you learn
all this stuff

253
00:15:19.695 --> 00:15:23.698
about Visenya and her
Valyrian Steel sword?

254
00:15:24.867 --> 00:15:26.601
From my father.

255
00:15:28.738 --> 00:15:32.207
He was a well-read
stonemason.

256
00:15:32.241 --> 00:15:36.512
Can't say I've ever met
a literate stonemason.

257
00:15:36.547 --> 00:15:39.316
Have you met many
stonemasons. My Lord?

258
00:15:41.753 --> 00:15:43.721
Careful now. girl.

259
00:15:43.755 --> 00:15:45.957
<i>I enjoy you. but be careful.</i>

260
00:15:45.991 --> 00:15:48.826
Take that back to the kitchen.

261
00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:50.628
Eat what you want.

262
00:15:53.731 --> 00:15:55.699
And. girl.

263
00:15:57.369 --> 00:15:59.470
M'lord.

264
00:16:01.039 --> 00:16:03.540
Lowborn girls say "M'lord."

265
00:16:03.575 --> 00:16:05.943
<i>not "My Lord."</i>

266
00:16:05.977 --> 00:16:08.212
If you're going
to pose as a commoner.

267
00:16:08.246 --> 00:16:10.381
you should do it properly.

268
00:16:11.883 --> 00:16:13.517
My mother served Lady Dustin

269
00:16:13.551 --> 00:16:16.486
for many years. My Lord.

270
00:16:16.521 --> 00:16:19.990
She taught me how to speak
proper... properly.

271
00:16:21.826 --> 00:16:23.594
You're too smart
for your own good.

272
00:16:23.628 --> 00:16:26.830
- <i>Has anyone told you that?</i>
- Yes.

273
00:16:27.865 --> 00:16:29.533
Go on.

274
00:16:40.778 --> 00:16:44.180
I beg pardon. Ser.

275
00:16:44.215 --> 00:16:46.516
I should have come to you after

276
00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:48.852
to thank you for saving me.

277
00:16:48.886 --> 00:16:51.221
- You were so brave.
- Brave?

278
00:16:51.255 --> 00:16:54.791
A dog doesn't need courage
to chase off rats.

279
00:16:54.825 --> 00:16:57.593
Does it give you joy
to scare people?

280
00:16:57.627 --> 00:17:00.530
No. It gives me joy
to kill people.

281
00:17:00.564 --> 00:17:02.831
Spare me.
You can't tell me

282
00:17:02.866 --> 00:17:05.834
Lord Eddard Stark of Winterfell
never killed a man.

283
00:17:05.868 --> 00:17:09.037
It was his duty.
He never liked it.

284
00:17:09.071 --> 00:17:11.139
Is that what he told you?

285
00:17:11.173 --> 00:17:13.607
He lied.

286
00:17:13.641 --> 00:17:16.577
Killing is the sweetest
thing there is.

287
00:17:16.611 --> 00:17:19.245
Why are you always so hateful?

288
00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.047
You'll be glad
of the hateful things I do

289
00:17:21.082 --> 00:17:23.850
someday when you're queen
and I'm all that stands

290
00:17:23.884 --> 00:17:26.353
between you
and your beloved king.

291
00:17:36.065 --> 00:17:37.599
I've demanded a meeting
of the Thirteen.

292
00:17:37.633 --> 00:17:39.434
One of them did this
or knows who did.

293
00:17:39.469 --> 00:17:41.036
You are one of the Thirteen.

294
00:17:41.071 --> 00:17:43.105
If I wanted your dragons.
I would have taken them.

295
00:17:43.139 --> 00:17:46.408
- They mean nothing to me on their own.
- Nothing?

296
00:17:46.442 --> 00:17:49.044
They're more valuable
than anything in the world.

297
00:17:49.078 --> 00:17:51.813
Shall we look inside my vault and see
what selling your dragons

298
00:17:51.847 --> 00:17:53.815
would buy me
I cannot buy already?

299
00:17:53.849 --> 00:17:55.983
We will get them back.

300
00:17:56.017 --> 00:17:57.851
There is no we.

301
00:17:57.886 --> 00:18:00.387
so why would you help me
get them back?

302
00:18:00.421 --> 00:18:02.188
I took you under my protection

303
00:18:02.223 --> 00:18:04.290
in front of the rulers
of my city.

304
00:18:04.325 --> 00:18:07.360
A man is what others
say he is and no more.

305
00:18:07.395 --> 00:18:09.997
If they say that
Xaro Xhoan Daxos is a liar.

306
00:18:10.032 --> 00:18:12.467
my word is worth nothing.

307
00:18:12.501 --> 00:18:15.070
I cannot let this thing
happen to you under my roof.

308
00:18:15.104 --> 00:18:17.473
But it did happen
under your roof.

309
00:18:17.507 --> 00:18:21.076
Khaleesi. many times
in my life I have been...

310
00:18:21.111 --> 00:18:22.845
I don't care where you've been.

311
00:18:45.466 --> 00:18:49.702
You think we're savages because
we don't live in stone castles.

312
00:18:49.737 --> 00:18:53.673
We can't make steel as good
as yours. it's true. but...

313
00:18:53.708 --> 00:18:56.242
We're free.

314
00:18:56.277 --> 00:18:58.069
If someone tried to tell us
we couldn't lie down

315
00:18:58.094 --> 00:18:59.546
as man and woman.

316
00:18:59.547 --> 00:19:02.115
we'd shove a spear up his ass.

317
00:19:02.149 --> 00:19:04.084
We don't go serving
some shit king

318
00:19:04.118 --> 00:19:05.685
who's only king
because his father was.

319
00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:09.123
No. No. you serve
Mance Rayder.

320
00:19:09.157 --> 00:19:10.557
the King-Beyond-the-Wall.

321
00:19:10.592 --> 00:19:13.494
We chose Mance Rayder
to lead us.

322
00:19:13.529 --> 00:19:15.897
He was a crow. same as you.

323
00:19:15.931 --> 00:19:18.199
but he wanted to be free.

324
00:19:19.469 --> 00:19:22.705
You could be free. too.

325
00:19:22.739 --> 00:19:24.339
You don't need to live
your whole life

326
00:19:24.374 --> 00:19:26.574
taking commands from old men.

327
00:19:26.608 --> 00:19:29.577
Wake up when you want
to wake up.

328
00:19:29.611 --> 00:19:32.513
I could show you the streams
to fish. the woods to hunt.

329
00:19:32.547 --> 00:19:36.749
<i>Build yourself a cabin and find</i>
<i>a woman to lie with in the night.</i>

330
00:19:38.585 --> 00:19:40.352
You're a pretty lad.

331
00:19:40.387 --> 00:19:43.755
The girls would claw each other's
eyes out to get naked with you.

332
00:19:46.225 --> 00:19:48.894
Walk.

333
00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.197
I could teach you how to do it.

334
00:19:52.232 --> 00:19:54.433
I know how to do it.

335
00:19:56.903 --> 00:20:00.273
You know nothing. Jon Snow.

336
00:20:21.128 --> 00:20:23.763
( Chatter )

337
00:20:28.935 --> 00:20:30.736
And what did she say?

338
00:20:30.771 --> 00:20:33.405
She admired your spirit.
Your Grace.

339
00:20:33.439 --> 00:20:35.440
And what then?

340
00:20:37.343 --> 00:20:39.612
She. uh...

341
00:20:39.646 --> 00:20:41.614
If every man
were held accountable

342
00:20:41.649 --> 00:20:43.616
for the actions
of every distant relative.

343
00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:46.819
Ser Alton. we'd all hang.

344
00:20:49.423 --> 00:20:53.192
She tore the paper
in half. Your Grace.

345
00:20:53.226 --> 00:20:54.727
You've acted with honor.

346
00:20:54.761 --> 00:20:56.829
I thank you for it.

347
00:20:56.863 --> 00:20:59.899
Lord Karstark. see that
Ser Alton's pen is clean.

348
00:20:59.933 --> 00:21:01.400
And give him a hot supper.

349
00:21:01.435 --> 00:21:03.904
Ser Alton's pen
is occupied. Your Grace.

350
00:21:03.938 --> 00:21:06.473
The prisoners
from the Yellow Fork.

351
00:21:06.508 --> 00:21:08.542
Too many prisoners.

352
00:21:08.577 --> 00:21:11.312
Is there room for Ser Alton?

353
00:21:11.347 --> 00:21:14.549
Does he need to lie down?

354
00:21:16.719 --> 00:21:18.821
Have the men
build him a new pen.

355
00:21:18.855 --> 00:21:21.490
<i>Put him in with</i>
<i>the Kingslayer for now.</i>

356
00:21:21.525 --> 00:21:23.693
Have your boy watch over them.

357
00:21:23.727 --> 00:21:26.362
Torrhen.

358
00:21:26.396 --> 00:21:28.030
That will be all.

359
00:21:34.704 --> 00:21:36.237
Your Grace.

360
00:21:36.272 --> 00:21:38.506
<i>A minute of your time?</i>

361
00:21:52.722 --> 00:21:54.957
I've been treating
your wounded men.

362
00:21:54.991 --> 00:21:57.603
And my enemies
as some of my bannermen

363
00:21:57.628 --> 00:21:59.295
are fond of mentioning.

364
00:21:59.296 --> 00:22:00.930
They're not my enemies.

365
00:22:00.964 --> 00:22:03.066
That's what I tell
my bannermen.

366
00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:05.802
I've already run through the
supplies I brought with me.

367
00:22:05.836 --> 00:22:07.236
Some are easily replaced...

368
00:22:07.271 --> 00:22:10.239
egg yolks. turpentine.
oil of roses.

369
00:22:10.273 --> 00:22:12.675
But some are not.

370
00:22:12.709 --> 00:22:15.777
I need silk for stitching.

371
00:22:17.246 --> 00:22:20.048
I need fennel root
for those with fever. willow bark.

372
00:22:20.082 --> 00:22:22.283
Mostly I need
milk of the poppy.

373
00:22:22.318 --> 00:22:25.486
You saw what it was like
to amputate a foot without any.

374
00:22:25.520 --> 00:22:27.533
I assume there will be
more loss of limb before

375
00:22:27.558 --> 00:22:29.123
this war is over.

376
00:22:29.124 --> 00:22:33.161
- If you need help finding these...
- I know where to find them.

377
00:22:34.297 --> 00:22:36.999
I'm sorry. I shouldn't
interrupt you.

378
00:22:37.033 --> 00:22:40.336
Continue. My Lady.

379
00:22:43.508 --> 00:22:45.403
You're riding to the Crag
to negotiate a surrender?

380
00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:47.318
Yes.

381
00:22:47.712 --> 00:22:50.881
The Crag will have a Maester
and he will have what I need.

382
00:22:50.948 --> 00:22:53.082
I expect he will.

383
00:22:53.117 --> 00:22:55.051
If I could write a list...

384
00:22:55.085 --> 00:22:57.486
come with me to the Crag.

385
00:22:58.988 --> 00:23:00.622
I don't think that will be...

386
00:23:00.657 --> 00:23:02.958
Let the Maester
show you his stores.

387
00:23:02.992 --> 00:23:07.128
I want the wounded men
to be treated well...

388
00:23:07.163 --> 00:23:09.064
all the wounded men.

389
00:23:12.202 --> 00:23:14.670
<i>( Dog barking )</i>

390
00:23:16.606 --> 00:23:19.141
Woman:
<i>Children. come inside. quick.</i>

391
00:23:19.176 --> 00:23:21.344
Hurry up!

392
00:23:21.378 --> 00:23:24.547
- <i>( Dog barking )</i>
- Man: <i>Can't find anything. Ser.</i>

393
00:23:24.582 --> 00:23:27.417
- They've lost the scent.
- Try again.

394
00:23:27.452 --> 00:23:29.019
We've circled
this farmhouse twice.

395
00:23:29.053 --> 00:23:30.654
There's no sign of them.

396
00:23:30.688 --> 00:23:34.558
We could start the search fresh
in the morning. My Lord.

397
00:23:34.592 --> 00:23:36.494
I'm looking at spending
the rest of life

398
00:23:36.528 --> 00:23:39.464
being treated like a fool and
a eunuch by my own people.

399
00:23:39.498 --> 00:23:41.499
Ask yourself. "Is there anything
I wouldn't do

400
00:23:41.533 --> 00:23:43.101
to stop that
from happening?"

401
00:23:43.135 --> 00:23:45.303
The hounds will find
the scent again.

402
00:23:45.337 --> 00:23:47.605
I'll beat them until they do.

403
00:23:47.639 --> 00:23:49.006
I'll whip every man here

404
00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:51.508
<i>until I have</i>
<i>both those boys in hand.</i>

405
00:23:51.542 --> 00:23:54.510
And once I've got them.
the pampered little shits...

406
00:23:56.113 --> 00:23:58.380
It's better to be
cruel than weak.

407
00:23:58.414 --> 00:24:00.648
Prince Theon.

408
00:24:00.683 --> 00:24:02.817
- Where are they?
- Who. m'lord?

409
00:24:02.851 --> 00:24:04.051
The Stark boys.
Where are they?

410
00:24:04.086 --> 00:24:06.320
I don't know.
I seen no one.

411
00:24:06.355 --> 00:24:08.256
Oh!

412
00:24:08.290 --> 00:24:09.724
Think harder.

413
00:24:09.759 --> 00:24:13.929
I swear. m'lord. I don't know.

414
00:24:13.964 --> 00:24:16.866
My Lord. over here.

415
00:24:19.570 --> 00:24:22.339
I think I've found
what we're looking for.

416
00:24:32.149 --> 00:24:34.384
Send the old man home.

417
00:24:39.622 --> 00:24:41.256
Go back to Winterfell.

418
00:24:41.291 --> 00:24:43.125
Take him back.

419
00:24:45.561 --> 00:24:47.863
Theon. don't do this.

420
00:24:51.801 --> 00:24:53.902
<i>( Birds chirping )</i>

421
00:25:06.316 --> 00:25:08.083
You came back.

422
00:25:08.117 --> 00:25:10.218
As soon as I heard.

423
00:25:10.253 --> 00:25:12.821
Do you know anything?

424
00:25:12.855 --> 00:25:15.891
- Irri is dead.
- <i>I know.</i>

425
00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:19.128
- She was a good...
- She's dead.

426
00:25:19.162 --> 00:25:20.930
She died alone.

427
00:25:20.964 --> 00:25:23.432
She died for me
and I couldn't protect her.

428
00:25:24.634 --> 00:25:26.202
Doreah?

429
00:25:26.236 --> 00:25:28.271
We can't find her.

430
00:25:29.573 --> 00:25:32.408
She must be dead. too.

431
00:25:32.443 --> 00:25:34.577
I led my people
out of the Red Waste

432
00:25:34.612 --> 00:25:36.179
and into the slaughterhouse.

433
00:25:36.213 --> 00:25:38.282
I should have been here.

434
00:25:39.317 --> 00:25:41.652
You went to find me a ship.

435
00:25:41.686 --> 00:25:43.854
My place is by your side.

436
00:25:43.889 --> 00:25:46.256
I shouldn't have left you
alone with these people.

437
00:25:46.291 --> 00:25:47.924
These people?

438
00:25:47.959 --> 00:25:50.426
They are not to be trusted.

439
00:25:50.461 --> 00:25:53.095
And who is to be trusted?

440
00:25:53.129 --> 00:25:54.696
Who are my people?

441
00:25:54.731 --> 00:25:56.932
The Targaryens?

442
00:25:56.966 --> 00:25:58.834
I only knew one...
my brother.

443
00:25:58.868 --> 00:26:01.069
and he would have let
1.000 men rape me

444
00:26:01.103 --> 00:26:03.171
if it had got him the crown.

445
00:26:03.205 --> 00:26:04.806
The Dothraki?

446
00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:07.029
Most of them turned on me
the day that Khal Drogo

447
00:26:07.054 --> 00:26:08.510
fell from his horse.

448
00:26:08.511 --> 00:26:10.278
Your people are in Westeros.

449
00:26:10.313 --> 00:26:13.014
The people in Westeros
don't know I'm alive.

450
00:26:13.048 --> 00:26:15.083
- They will soon enough.
- And then what?

451
00:26:15.118 --> 00:26:17.319
They'll pray for my return?

452
00:26:17.354 --> 00:26:19.822
They'll wave dragon banners
and shout my name?

453
00:26:19.857 --> 00:26:22.993
That's what my brother believed
and he was a fool.

454
00:26:23.027 --> 00:26:25.462
You are not your brother.

455
00:26:25.496 --> 00:26:28.064
Trust me. Khaleesi.

456
00:26:28.099 --> 00:26:30.233
There it is...

457
00:26:30.268 --> 00:26:32.502
"trust me."

458
00:26:32.536 --> 00:26:35.138
And it's you I should trust.
Ser Jorah?

459
00:26:35.172 --> 00:26:37.106
Only you?

460
00:26:39.843 --> 00:26:43.245
I don't need trust any longer.

461
00:26:43.279 --> 00:26:46.114
I don't want it and I don't have
room for it.

462
00:26:46.148 --> 00:26:48.283
You are too young to be so...

463
00:26:48.317 --> 00:26:50.519
And you are too familiar.

464
00:26:54.958 --> 00:26:57.426
Forgive me. Khaleesi.

465
00:26:59.029 --> 00:27:02.132
No one can survive
in this world without help.

466
00:27:02.166 --> 00:27:03.600
No one.

467
00:27:03.635 --> 00:27:06.237
Let me help you. please.

468
00:27:06.271 --> 00:27:09.039
Tell me how.

469
00:27:10.475 --> 00:27:12.342
Find my dragons.

470
00:27:20.118 --> 00:27:22.920
Ygritte: How long till we get
back to your crows?

471
00:27:24.322 --> 00:27:26.056
We're close.

472
00:27:26.091 --> 00:27:29.594
What. a day?
A half-day?

473
00:27:33.532 --> 00:27:36.200
You don't know. do you?

474
00:27:36.235 --> 00:27:39.137
- Do you even know where they are?
- We're close.

475
00:27:40.907 --> 00:27:43.141
What do you think they'll say
when they hear about you and me?

476
00:27:43.176 --> 00:27:45.244
Nothing happened
between you and me.

477
00:27:45.278 --> 00:27:48.648
"I swear it.
old master king crow. Ser.

478
00:27:48.682 --> 00:27:51.417
we were only close
together for warmth.

479
00:27:51.451 --> 00:27:53.053
And then I felt it.

480
00:27:53.087 --> 00:27:55.789
right up against
me backside like a club.

481
00:27:55.823 --> 00:27:58.291
I can show you the bruise
on me tailbone.

482
00:27:58.326 --> 00:28:01.761
And before I knew
what was where. his... his...

483
00:28:01.796 --> 00:28:04.731
well. it was all out in the open.
all angry as you like.

484
00:28:04.799 --> 00:28:08.802
And I didn't want to want it.
but. oh. I did!

485
00:28:08.836 --> 00:28:11.804
And he spread me legs
and... ruined.

486
00:28:11.838 --> 00:28:13.506
The shame of it.

487
00:28:13.541 --> 00:28:15.675
Now I can never marry
a perfumed lord.

488
00:28:15.710 --> 00:28:17.405
What will me poor
savage father say?"

489
00:28:17.430 --> 00:28:19.379
Turn back around.

490
00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:21.515
"And I thought that we were done.
but he said.

491
00:28:21.549 --> 00:28:24.285
( deep voice )
'Turn back around.'"

492
00:28:24.319 --> 00:28:26.987
( normal voice )
I'll tell you what. Jon Snow.

493
00:28:27.022 --> 00:28:29.123
since it's going to be
your word against mine.

494
00:28:29.157 --> 00:28:33.026
and since you can't talk
about it without blushing.

495
00:28:33.061 --> 00:28:36.130
we may as well just.

496
00:28:37.065 --> 00:28:39.199
What. right here in the muck?

497
00:28:39.234 --> 00:28:41.435
I'll keep you warm enough.

498
00:28:43.405 --> 00:28:45.506
Are you that afraid of it?

499
00:28:45.540 --> 00:28:47.041
That's enough.

500
00:28:47.075 --> 00:28:49.510
Oh. it's nice

501
00:28:49.544 --> 00:28:52.579
and wet and warm.

502
00:28:52.614 --> 00:28:54.415
Enough

503
00:28:55.550 --> 00:28:57.318
it don't have teeth.

504
00:29:05.226 --> 00:29:06.627
All right!

505
00:29:07.495 --> 00:29:09.129
All right.

506
00:29:10.565 --> 00:29:12.198
Gods. you're dull.

507
00:29:13.768 --> 00:29:16.336
( Grunting )

508
00:29:22.375 --> 00:29:24.176
<i>( Sword rings )</i>

509
00:29:35.288 --> 00:29:37.222
<i>( Ygritte whistles )</i>

510
00:29:48.336 --> 00:29:50.871
Should have took me
while you had the chance.

511
00:29:58.882 --> 00:30:01.250
<i>( Sansa crying )</i>

512
00:30:01.284 --> 00:30:03.486
<i>( Sansa crying ) No. no!</i>

513
00:30:10.894 --> 00:30:12.661
- ( Screams )
- ( Laughs )

514
00:30:12.696 --> 00:30:14.763
( Screams )

515
00:30:22.737 --> 00:30:26.039
No. Oh. no.

516
00:30:35.917 --> 00:30:38.753
( Whimpering )

517
00:30:41.824 --> 00:30:44.192
It's all right.
Give me that.

518
00:30:44.227 --> 00:30:48.463
If the queen sees I can have
Joffrey's children now...

519
00:30:48.498 --> 00:30:50.232
Help me flip it over.

520
00:31:06.948 --> 00:31:09.783
- Where are you going?
- To tell her Grace.

521
00:31:11.686 --> 00:31:13.787
You'll say nothing to anyone.

522
00:31:13.821 --> 00:31:15.922
Do you understand?

523
00:31:36.078 --> 00:31:39.413
Your mother might have
prepared you.

524
00:31:39.448 --> 00:31:41.816
You flowered. my dear.
No more.

525
00:31:41.850 --> 00:31:45.019
My mother told me. but I
thought it would be different.

526
00:31:45.054 --> 00:31:46.554
In what way?

527
00:31:46.589 --> 00:31:49.758
I thought it would be less...

528
00:31:49.793 --> 00:31:52.895
less messy.

529
00:31:52.929 --> 00:31:55.698
Wait until you bear the child.

530
00:31:57.401 --> 00:31:58.835
You're a woman now.

531
00:31:58.869 --> 00:32:01.938
Do you have any idea
what that means?

532
00:32:01.973 --> 00:32:04.474
I'm fit to bear children
for the king?

533
00:32:04.509 --> 00:32:06.944
A prospect that
once delighted you...

534
00:32:06.978 --> 00:32:09.413
bringing little princes
and princesses into the world.

535
00:32:09.447 --> 00:32:13.149
the greatest honor for a queen.

536
00:32:17.554 --> 00:32:20.522
Joffrey has always
been difficult.

537
00:32:20.556 --> 00:32:22.657
Even his birth.
I labored a day and a half

538
00:32:22.691 --> 00:32:24.759
to bring him into this world.

539
00:32:24.793 --> 00:32:27.228
You cannot imagine the pain.

540
00:32:27.263 --> 00:32:29.164
I screamed so loudly.
I was sure

541
00:32:29.198 --> 00:32:30.666
Robert would hear me
in the Kingswood.

542
00:32:30.700 --> 00:32:33.735
His Grace was not with you?

543
00:32:33.769 --> 00:32:35.270
Robert was hunting.

544
00:32:35.305 --> 00:32:37.173
That was his custom.

545
00:32:39.810 --> 00:32:42.512
Whenever my time was near.

546
00:32:42.547 --> 00:32:45.149
my royal husband
would flee to the trees

547
00:32:45.183 --> 00:32:50.020
with his huntsmen
and his hounds.

548
00:32:50.054 --> 00:32:51.588
And when he returned.
he would present me

549
00:32:51.622 --> 00:32:54.824
with some pelts
or a stag's head.

550
00:32:54.858 --> 00:32:56.725
and I would present him
with a baby.

551
00:32:58.494 --> 00:33:01.163
Not that I wanted
him there. mind you.

552
00:33:01.197 --> 00:33:04.232
I had Grand Maester Pycelle.
an army of midwives.

553
00:33:04.266 --> 00:33:06.234
and I had my brother.

554
00:33:06.268 --> 00:33:09.605
When they told Jaime he wasn't
allowed in the birthing room.

555
00:33:09.639 --> 00:33:12.975
he smiled and asked
which one of them

556
00:33:13.010 --> 00:33:15.143
proposed to keep him out.

557
00:33:18.248 --> 00:33:20.817
Joffrey will show you
no such devotion.

558
00:33:23.187 --> 00:33:25.756
You may never love the king.

559
00:33:25.790 --> 00:33:27.657
but you will love his children.

560
00:33:27.692 --> 00:33:31.061
I love his Grace
with all my heart.

561
00:33:31.095 --> 00:33:33.963
That's so very
touching to hear.

562
00:33:38.468 --> 00:33:40.736
Permit me to share
some womanly wisdom with you

563
00:33:40.770 --> 00:33:43.772
on this very special day.

564
00:33:43.806 --> 00:33:47.608
The more people you love.
the weaker you are.

565
00:33:47.642 --> 00:33:51.212
You'll do things for them that
you know you shouldn't do.

566
00:33:51.246 --> 00:33:54.949
You'll act the fool to make them
happy. to keep them safe.

567
00:33:57.319 --> 00:34:00.187
Love no one but your children.

568
00:34:00.221 --> 00:34:03.790
On that front.
a mother has no choice.

569
00:34:03.824 --> 00:34:08.462
But... shouldn't
I love Joffrey. Your Grace?

570
00:34:10.932 --> 00:34:13.634
You can try.

571
00:34:13.669 --> 00:34:15.637
little dove.

572
00:34:21.410 --> 00:34:23.545
<i>( Chatter )</i>

573
00:34:31.521 --> 00:34:34.156
Who did you say
your mother was again?

574
00:34:34.190 --> 00:34:35.957
Cinda Lannister.

575
00:34:35.991 --> 00:34:37.759
Is she the fat one?

576
00:34:39.161 --> 00:34:40.528
Well. perhaps she's gotten
a little larger than she...

577
00:34:40.562 --> 00:34:44.331
No. no. There's only one
fat Lannister.

578
00:34:44.366 --> 00:34:47.235
If she was your mother.
you'd know it.

579
00:34:48.971 --> 00:34:52.040
I... I squired
for you once. you know?

580
00:34:53.209 --> 00:34:54.676
When?

581
00:34:54.710 --> 00:34:58.113
The tournament the day
of Willem Frey's wedding.

582
00:34:58.148 --> 00:35:01.184
I went to
Willem Frey's wedding?

583
00:35:01.218 --> 00:35:03.019
<i>You did.</i>

584
00:35:03.053 --> 00:35:05.488
Your squire had gotten
so drunk the night before that he...

585
00:35:05.523 --> 00:35:07.657
He threw up on his horse

586
00:35:07.691 --> 00:35:09.225
on the way
to the tourney grounds.

587
00:35:09.259 --> 00:35:11.794
- What was his name?
- Bryan.

588
00:35:11.828 --> 00:35:14.996
( Laughs ) Poor lad.

589
00:35:15.031 --> 00:35:18.033
That was my brother's doing.
I seem to recall.

590
00:35:20.235 --> 00:35:22.403
I remember you.

591
00:35:22.437 --> 00:35:25.305
You had never squired
for anyone before.

592
00:35:25.339 --> 00:35:27.274
That's right.
I ran up and volunteered.

593
00:35:27.308 --> 00:35:30.677
"Let me. My Lord.
Let me."

594
00:35:30.711 --> 00:35:33.146
My father was furious.

595
00:35:33.181 --> 00:35:34.915
afraid I'd embarrass our family

596
00:35:34.949 --> 00:35:37.383
in front of <i>the</i> family.

597
00:35:39.486 --> 00:35:40.953
You didn't. though.

598
00:35:40.988 --> 00:35:43.455
- You really remember?
- Mm.

599
00:35:43.490 --> 00:35:45.991
You knew when you were needed
and when to go away.

600
00:35:46.025 --> 00:35:47.559
It's a rare talent.

601
00:35:47.593 --> 00:35:51.362
Most of my squires.
they mean well.

602
00:35:51.397 --> 00:35:54.833
but young men with big jobs.
they tend to overdo them.

603
00:35:54.867 --> 00:35:56.734
Well. when I think
back to that day...

604
00:35:56.769 --> 00:35:58.536
( hisses )

605
00:36:06.644 --> 00:36:08.545
You were saying?

606
00:36:08.579 --> 00:36:10.982
I...

607
00:36:11.016 --> 00:36:13.918
never mind.
It's embarrassing.

608
00:36:13.953 --> 00:36:16.655
More embarrassing
than being chained to a post

609
00:36:16.689 --> 00:36:18.457
covered in your own shit?

610
00:36:19.893 --> 00:36:22.462
I remember everything
about that day...

611
00:36:22.496 --> 00:36:24.831
your helmet. your horse.

612
00:36:24.866 --> 00:36:27.567
the rake line in the dirt
along the list.

613
00:36:27.602 --> 00:36:29.069
where the sun was in the sky

614
00:36:29.103 --> 00:36:31.304
when you knocked
Balon Swann from his horse.

615
00:36:31.339 --> 00:36:34.541
and the dent in your shield
when you handed it back to me.

616
00:36:36.610 --> 00:36:39.512
I'll remember it all
until I die.

617
00:36:41.148 --> 00:36:43.049
That was the best day
of my life.

618
00:36:45.952 --> 00:36:49.989
And I remember being on the field
after it was over.

619
00:36:50.023 --> 00:36:51.491
All the competitors were done.

620
00:36:51.525 --> 00:36:53.527
I was the last one out there.

621
00:36:55.630 --> 00:36:58.298
And I couldn't leave.

622
00:36:58.333 --> 00:37:00.601
<i>I couldn't bring myself</i>
<i>to go and sit with my family</i>

623
00:37:00.635 --> 00:37:02.803
at a table so far
on the edge of the feast

624
00:37:02.837 --> 00:37:05.172
you could barely
even see the bride.

625
00:37:05.207 --> 00:37:07.640
And I couldn't bear to tell them
what it had been like squiring for you

626
00:37:08.610 --> 00:37:10.157
when I knew that they could
never have the faintest idea

627
00:37:10.182 --> 00:37:11.473
what I was talking about.

628
00:37:13.448 --> 00:37:15.449
I understand completely.

629
00:37:15.484 --> 00:37:18.519
How could you?

630
00:37:18.554 --> 00:37:21.456
S-sorry. I... I didn't
mean to doubt you.

631
00:37:21.490 --> 00:37:24.992
- It's just that I...
- I was 16 once.

632
00:37:25.027 --> 00:37:28.496
I also had to replace someone's
squire on short notice.

633
00:37:28.530 --> 00:37:30.198
Which knight was it?

634
00:37:30.232 --> 00:37:33.000
Barristan Selmy.

635
00:37:34.469 --> 00:37:36.270
The fight against
the Kingswood outlaws.

636
00:37:36.304 --> 00:37:38.973
Before your time.

637
00:37:39.007 --> 00:37:40.508
What was he like?

638
00:37:40.542 --> 00:37:43.277
( Sighs )

639
00:37:43.311 --> 00:37:46.748
He was

640
00:37:46.782 --> 00:37:49.617
a painter.

641
00:37:49.651 --> 00:37:52.954
a painter who only used red.

642
00:37:55.424 --> 00:37:59.528
I couldn't imagine being
able to fight like that.

643
00:37:59.562 --> 00:38:01.764
not back then.

644
00:38:01.798 --> 00:38:04.154
And to help him do that.
to be a part of something

645
00:38:04.179 --> 00:38:06.179
that perfect...

646
00:38:08.405 --> 00:38:10.974
I don't need to explain
how that felt. not to you.

647
00:38:11.976 --> 00:38:13.677
It's hard to put into words.

648
00:38:13.711 --> 00:38:16.847
It's like stepping into a dream

649
00:38:16.881 --> 00:38:20.050
you've been dreaming
for as long as you can remember

650
00:38:20.085 --> 00:38:21.919
and finding out that the dream

651
00:38:21.953 --> 00:38:24.989
is more real than your life.

652
00:38:27.426 --> 00:38:30.529
Leaving that battlefield was

653
00:38:30.563 --> 00:38:32.664
like being dragged off
to prison.

654
00:38:32.699 --> 00:38:36.068
- Did you squire for him again?
- No.

655
00:38:37.171 --> 00:38:39.839
I didn't have your gift.

656
00:38:39.874 --> 00:38:43.210
He couldn't take a step
without stepping on me.

657
00:38:43.244 --> 00:38:46.546
I was awful.
a complete liability...

658
00:38:46.580 --> 00:38:50.183
until one of the outlaws

659
00:38:50.217 --> 00:38:53.786
decided to take on
a 16-year-old squire.

660
00:38:59.459 --> 00:39:02.026
It's a good thing
I am who I am.

661
00:39:02.061 --> 00:39:05.730
( Chuckles ) I'd have been useless
at anything else.

662
00:39:10.303 --> 00:39:13.371
I'm not well-suited
for imprisonment.

663
00:39:13.406 --> 00:39:15.107
Shocking. I know.

664
00:39:15.141 --> 00:39:16.842
Some men are.

665
00:39:16.876 --> 00:39:20.379
Ned Stark...
I imagine he made

666
00:39:20.414 --> 00:39:23.850
an excellent prisoner
right up until the end.

667
00:39:23.885 --> 00:39:27.353
But me. though...
my life has left me

668
00:39:27.388 --> 00:39:30.423
uniquely unfit for constraint.

669
00:39:32.125 --> 00:39:33.592
Have you thought about...?

670
00:39:33.626 --> 00:39:35.227
Of course.

671
00:39:35.261 --> 00:39:38.130
- Every day.
- And?

672
00:39:39.865 --> 00:39:44.302
Good prisoners breed
good jailers. apparently.

673
00:39:44.336 --> 00:39:46.471
The Starks are very careful.

674
00:39:47.673 --> 00:39:51.810
But there is a way. I think.

675
00:39:51.845 --> 00:39:54.480
It wasn't possible until now.

676
00:39:54.514 --> 00:39:57.717
What is it?

677
00:40:01.856 --> 00:40:04.825
- It's actually quite simple.
- Well. let me help you.

678
00:40:04.860 --> 00:40:07.661
You'll only have
to do one thing.

679
00:40:07.696 --> 00:40:09.563
Tell me.

680
00:40:12.167 --> 00:40:14.268
You'll have to die.

681
00:40:25.579 --> 00:40:27.680
<i>( Crunching )</i>

682
00:40:44.866 --> 00:40:47.401
( Choking )

683
00:40:51.105 --> 00:40:53.539
( Bone breaks )

684
00:40:59.079 --> 00:41:01.948
<i>( Bird screeching )</i>

685
00:41:07.454 --> 00:41:10.089
Jorah the Andal.

686
00:41:10.123 --> 00:41:13.225
This man must sail
past old Valyria.

687
00:41:13.259 --> 00:41:17.563
All who travel too close to
the Doom must have protection.

688
00:41:17.597 --> 00:41:19.498
I didn't come here for lessons.

689
00:41:19.533 --> 00:41:21.801
No. you came for the dragons.

690
00:41:21.835 --> 00:41:23.903
You have them?

691
00:41:25.105 --> 00:41:27.073
Where are they?

692
00:41:27.107 --> 00:41:29.108
Draw your sword.

693
00:41:29.142 --> 00:41:32.811
See what your steel is worth.

694
00:41:35.449 --> 00:41:39.418
You want to please
the Mother of Dragons.

695
00:41:44.224 --> 00:41:46.825
You love her.

696
00:41:49.763 --> 00:41:51.930
Where are the dragons?

697
00:41:53.299 --> 00:41:55.834
Will you betray her again.
Jorah the Andal?

698
00:42:00.406 --> 00:42:03.241
Will you betray her again?

699
00:42:05.411 --> 00:42:07.112
Never.

700
00:42:12.884 --> 00:42:15.118
<i>The thief you seek</i>

701
00:42:15.153 --> 00:42:18.120
is with her now.

702
00:42:22.559 --> 00:42:24.893
Spice King: <i>I did not leave</i>
<i>the comfort of my home</i>

703
00:42:24.927 --> 00:42:26.694
to come to yours
and be called a thief.

704
00:42:26.729 --> 00:42:28.663
No one is calling you a thief.

705
00:42:28.697 --> 00:42:30.398
Who is she to accuse us?

706
00:42:30.433 --> 00:42:32.434
Please. they're my children.

707
00:42:32.468 --> 00:42:34.736
- I'm begging you.
- Begging us?

708
00:42:34.770 --> 00:42:37.205
It wasn't very long ago
you were threatening us.

709
00:42:37.239 --> 00:42:39.941
Without me.
the dragons will die.

710
00:42:39.976 --> 00:42:42.043
It will be for the best.

711
00:42:42.078 --> 00:42:44.346
<i>Your dragons</i>
<i>will bring the world</i>

712
00:42:44.380 --> 00:42:47.149
nothing but death
and misery. my dear.

713
00:42:47.183 --> 00:42:49.585
If I knew where they were.
I would not tell you.

714
00:42:49.619 --> 00:42:51.554
Pyat Pree:
<i>You are cruel. my friend.</i>

715
00:42:51.588 --> 00:42:54.557
The mother of dragons
is in the right.

716
00:42:54.592 --> 00:42:57.728
<i>She must be reunited</i>
<i>with her babies.</i>

717
00:42:57.762 --> 00:43:01.632
- I will help you. Khaleesi.
- How?

718
00:43:01.666 --> 00:43:05.336
I will take you
to the House of the Undying

719
00:43:05.371 --> 00:43:07.338
where I have put them.

720
00:43:08.373 --> 00:43:10.508
You have my dragons?

721
00:43:10.542 --> 00:43:12.811
When I learned you were
coming to our city.

722
00:43:12.845 --> 00:43:15.547
I made an arrangement
with the King of Qarth.

723
00:43:15.581 --> 00:43:17.582
( Laughter )

724
00:43:17.616 --> 00:43:18.983
He procured them for me.

725
00:43:19.018 --> 00:43:21.987
- But there is no King of Qarth.
- Xaro: There is now.

726
00:43:22.021 --> 00:43:24.222
That was the other half
of the arrangement.

727
00:43:26.459 --> 00:43:29.528
<i>You would keep your gates</i>
<i>and your minds closed</i>

728
00:43:29.562 --> 00:43:32.699
to everything
outside your walls.

729
00:43:32.733 --> 00:43:35.835
but Qarth cannot remain
the greatest city that ever was

730
00:43:35.870 --> 00:43:37.504
if it refuses to change.

731
00:43:37.538 --> 00:43:40.174
I will open Qarth to the world

732
00:43:40.208 --> 00:43:44.479
as I have forced it
to open itself to me.

733
00:43:44.513 --> 00:43:47.448
Your ambition
is an inspiration.

734
00:43:47.483 --> 00:43:50.518
But like all upstarts.
you overreach.

735
00:43:50.552 --> 00:43:53.287
Three dragons the size of cats

736
00:43:53.322 --> 00:43:55.623
and an alliance
with a charlatan

737
00:43:55.657 --> 00:43:58.159
do not make you a king.

738
00:43:58.193 --> 00:44:00.394
An upstart and a charlatan?

739
00:44:00.429 --> 00:44:03.464
<i>Empires have been</i>
<i>built by less.</i>

740
00:44:03.498 --> 00:44:06.934
Those on the margins
often come to control the center.

741
00:44:06.968 --> 00:44:09.302
and those in the center
make room for them.

742
00:44:09.337 --> 00:44:11.037
<i>willingly or otherwise.</i>

743
00:44:15.375 --> 00:44:18.744
The Mother of Dragons
will be with her babies.

744
00:44:20.313 --> 00:44:21.847
She will give them her love

745
00:44:21.882 --> 00:44:24.650
and they will thrive
by her side...

746
00:44:27.186 --> 00:44:28.887
forever.

747
00:44:48.743 --> 00:44:51.245
A mother should be
with her children.

748
00:44:54.383 --> 00:44:57.052
Where will you run to.
Daenerys Stormborn?

749
00:44:57.086 --> 00:45:00.389
Your dragons wait for you
in the House of the Undying.

750
00:45:00.423 --> 00:45:02.726
Come see them.

751
00:45:11.603 --> 00:45:13.871
- Lady Stark!
- No farther.

752
00:45:13.905 --> 00:45:15.639
Keep your hands off me. woman.

753
00:45:15.673 --> 00:45:19.343
Don't enter without
an invitation. <i>man.</i>

754
00:45:20.712 --> 00:45:22.813
Forgive me.
Lady Stark.

755
00:45:22.847 --> 00:45:25.516
- Catelyn: <i>What is it?</i>
- They caught the Kingslayer.

756
00:45:28.653 --> 00:45:31.388
( Men shouting )

757
00:45:31.390 --> 00:45:34.124
- Kill the fucking Kingslayer!
- Hang him!

758
00:45:34.192 --> 00:45:37.761
( Men shouting )

759
00:45:37.796 --> 00:45:39.630
You'll die today.

760
00:45:39.664 --> 00:45:42.132
Justice for the Karstark.

761
00:45:55.280 --> 00:45:56.915
Gut him!

762
00:46:09.461 --> 00:46:11.830
Get back!
I want his head!

763
00:46:13.099 --> 00:46:15.500
Any man who stands
between a father

764
00:46:15.534 --> 00:46:18.036
and his vengeance
asks for death.

765
00:46:18.070 --> 00:46:20.305
Lord Karstark.

766
00:46:20.339 --> 00:46:23.241
this man is our prisoner.

767
00:46:23.275 --> 00:46:25.176
This monster killed my son.

768
00:46:25.211 --> 00:46:27.246
And crippled mine.

769
00:46:27.280 --> 00:46:29.047
He will answer for his crimes.

770
00:46:29.082 --> 00:46:31.115
<i>I promise you. but not here.</i>

771
00:46:31.150 --> 00:46:33.452
I will have his head.
And if you try and stop me...

772
00:46:33.486 --> 00:46:35.887
You will strike me down?

773
00:46:35.921 --> 00:46:38.223
Have you forgotten me. Ser?

774
00:46:38.257 --> 00:46:40.325
<I>I am the widow of your</I>
<I>liege Lord Eddard Stark.</I>

775
00:46:40.359 --> 00:46:41.860
I am the mother of your king!

776
00:46:41.894 --> 00:46:44.729
- And where is our king now?
- You know very well.

777
00:46:44.764 --> 00:46:46.899
He has gone to the Crag
to accept the surrender.

778
00:46:46.933 --> 00:46:50.669
Aye. gone to the Crag.
but not to negotiate.

779
00:46:50.703 --> 00:46:52.604
He brought that
foreign bitch with him.

780
00:46:52.639 --> 00:46:53.446
How dare you?

781
00:46:53.471 --> 00:46:55.592
Threatening My Lady
is an act of treason.

782
00:46:55.676 --> 00:46:56.876
Treason?

783
00:46:56.910 --> 00:46:58.678
How can it be treason
to kill Lannisters?

784
00:46:58.712 --> 00:47:00.780
I understand
your grief. My Lord...

785
00:47:00.815 --> 00:47:03.249
better than most
I understand it...

786
00:47:03.283 --> 00:47:06.219
but in the name of my son.
the King in the North.

787
00:47:06.254 --> 00:47:08.288
stand down.

788
00:47:09.824 --> 00:47:11.591
When your son returns.

789
00:47:11.626 --> 00:47:14.027
<i>I will demand</i>
<i>this murderer's head.</i>

790
00:47:14.061 --> 00:47:16.296
Wise men do not
make demands of kings.

791
00:47:16.330 --> 00:47:19.532
Fathers who love their sons do.

792
00:47:19.566 --> 00:47:21.901
I will have his head.

793
00:47:23.403 --> 00:47:27.306
Thank you for fighting
on my behalf. Lady Stark.

794
00:47:27.340 --> 00:47:29.174
I would have come
to your defense. but...

795
00:47:29.209 --> 00:47:31.876
Take him to the stockades.

796
00:47:31.911 --> 00:47:34.112
Bind him with every chain
you can find!

797
00:47:34.146 --> 00:47:35.646
You've become a real she-wolf
in your later years.

798
00:47:35.681 --> 00:47:37.849
There's not much fish
left in you.

799
00:47:37.883 --> 00:47:39.584
And gag him!

800
00:47:43.855 --> 00:47:46.957
Since when do you light
your own candles?

801
00:47:46.991 --> 00:47:49.326
Since I decided that
I can't stand to look

802
00:47:49.361 --> 00:47:52.896
at any of my handmaidens
for another instant.

803
00:47:54.266 --> 00:47:57.368
How many times can you
read one raven scroll?

804
00:47:57.402 --> 00:48:01.072
Stannis Baratheon's fleet
has been spotted sailing north

805
00:48:01.106 --> 00:48:03.742
past Tarth... 200 ships.

806
00:48:03.776 --> 00:48:07.913
- More than we have.
- Yes. that's more than we have.

807
00:48:07.947 --> 00:48:10.315
He'll be at our gates
within five days.

808
00:48:10.349 --> 00:48:12.050
four if he has the wind.

809
00:48:12.085 --> 00:48:14.820
We have strong. high walls.

810
00:48:14.854 --> 00:48:17.923
We'll rain fire
down on them from above.

811
00:48:17.957 --> 00:48:20.092
"Rain fire on them
from above."

812
00:48:20.126 --> 00:48:21.960
You're quoting father.
aren't you?

813
00:48:21.994 --> 00:48:23.428
Why not?

814
00:48:23.463 --> 00:48:25.363
He has a good mind
for strategy. doesn't he?

815
00:48:25.398 --> 00:48:28.166
We call it tactics.
not strategy.

816
00:48:28.200 --> 00:48:30.335
But. yes. he does have
a good mind for it.

817
00:48:30.369 --> 00:48:32.204
The best mind. some would say.

818
00:48:32.238 --> 00:48:34.206
Sadly. he's not here.

819
00:48:35.174 --> 00:48:37.509
It's just you. me. and Joffrey.

820
00:48:37.543 --> 00:48:39.711
the Lord of the Seven Kingdoms

821
00:48:39.746 --> 00:48:41.513
and protector of the realm.

822
00:48:43.283 --> 00:48:44.983
I'm sure you'll make
a point eventually.

823
00:48:45.017 --> 00:48:48.386
He needs to start
acting like a king.

824
00:48:48.421 --> 00:48:51.589
This war you started
is coming to our doorstep.

825
00:48:51.624 --> 00:48:53.925
And if the entire city
wants Joffrey dead...

826
00:48:53.959 --> 00:48:56.227
I'm not the one giving
the boy whores to abuse.

827
00:48:56.261 --> 00:48:58.362
I thought the girls
might help him.

828
00:48:58.396 --> 00:49:00.797
- Did you?
- <i>I was wrong.</i>

829
00:49:03.533 --> 00:49:06.101
If we can't control him...

830
00:49:06.136 --> 00:49:07.736
Do you think I haven't tried?

831
00:49:10.173 --> 00:49:12.975
He doesn't listen to me.

832
00:49:14.678 --> 00:49:17.713
It's hard to put
a leash on a dog

833
00:49:17.747 --> 00:49:20.482
once you've put
a crown on its head.

834
00:49:23.686 --> 00:49:26.521
I always hoped
he'd be like Jaime.

835
00:49:28.591 --> 00:49:30.826
He looks like him...

836
00:49:33.865 --> 00:49:36.566
in a certain light.

837
00:49:38.903 --> 00:49:40.905
The boy is more
Robert than Jaime.

838
00:49:40.939 --> 00:49:44.909
Robert was a drunken fool.
but he didn't enjoy cruelty.

839
00:49:46.845 --> 00:49:50.014
Sometimes I wonder...

840
00:49:50.048 --> 00:49:52.449
What?

841
00:49:52.484 --> 00:49:55.886
If this is the price

842
00:49:55.920 --> 00:50:00.256
for what we've done.
for our sins.

843
00:50:00.290 --> 00:50:02.325
Sins?

844
00:50:02.359 --> 00:50:03.893
The Targaryens...

845
00:50:03.927 --> 00:50:05.506
Wed brother and sister
for hundreds of years.

846
00:50:05.531 --> 00:50:07.531
I know.

847
00:50:09.233 --> 00:50:12.802
That's what Jaime and I would say to
each other in our moments of doubt.

848
00:50:12.837 --> 00:50:16.807
It's what I told Ned Stark when he
was stupid enough to confront me.

849
00:50:18.777 --> 00:50:21.980
Half the Targaryens
went mad. didn't they?

850
00:50:22.014 --> 00:50:23.415
What's the saying?

851
00:50:23.449 --> 00:50:27.986
Every time a Targaryen is born.
the Gods flip a coin.

852
00:50:28.020 --> 00:50:30.522
You've beaten the odds.

853
00:50:30.556 --> 00:50:33.157
Tommen and Myrcella
are good. decent children.

854
00:50:33.192 --> 00:50:35.026
both of them.

855
00:50:37.128 --> 00:50:39.263
( Crying )

856
00:51:02.485 --> 00:51:05.286
- Why wait?
- We're sworn to the king.

857
00:51:05.321 --> 00:51:08.089
- There's not a king.
- That's treason.

858
00:51:08.124 --> 00:51:10.291
So is saving Lannisters. yeah?

859
00:51:10.325 --> 00:51:13.093
- Back off. you.
- No. I won't.

860
00:51:13.128 --> 00:51:15.629
Your son returns
at dawn. My Lady?

861
00:51:15.664 --> 00:51:17.231
So they say.

862
00:51:17.265 --> 00:51:20.101
Brienne: <i>The Kingslayer</i>
<i>won't last the night.</i>

863
00:51:20.135 --> 00:51:22.469
<i>The more they drink.</i>
<i>the angrier they'll get.</i>

864
00:51:23.705 --> 00:51:25.872
And when the Karstarks
draw their swords...

865
00:51:25.907 --> 00:51:29.342
<i>who wants to die</i>
<i>defending a Lannister?</i>

866
00:51:30.311 --> 00:51:31.946
Come.

867
00:51:47.831 --> 00:51:50.232
I need to be alone with him.

868
00:51:50.267 --> 00:51:54.136
- My Lady. our orders...
- Your orders. which I just gave you.

869
00:51:54.170 --> 00:51:56.738
are to leave me alone with him.

870
00:52:01.644 --> 00:52:03.878
Come to say goodbye.
Lady Stark?

871
00:52:03.913 --> 00:52:08.717
I believe it's my last night
in this world.

872
00:52:08.752 --> 00:52:10.185
Is that a woman?

873
00:52:10.220 --> 00:52:12.988
Do you hear them out there?

874
00:52:13.023 --> 00:52:15.658
They want your head.

875
00:52:15.692 --> 00:52:19.161
Well. old Lord Karstark
doesn't seem to like me.

876
00:52:19.195 --> 00:52:22.431
You strangled his son
with your chains.

877
00:52:22.466 --> 00:52:24.734
Oh. oh.

878
00:52:24.801 --> 00:52:26.402
Was he the one on guard duty?

879
00:52:26.436 --> 00:52:28.971
<i>( Sighs )</i>

880
00:52:29.006 --> 00:52:30.807
He was in my way.

881
00:52:30.841 --> 00:52:32.441
Any Knight would have
done the same.

882
00:52:32.476 --> 00:52:34.644
You are no Knight.

883
00:52:34.678 --> 00:52:37.247
You have forsaken
every vow you ever took.

884
00:52:37.281 --> 00:52:39.048
So many vows.

885
00:52:39.083 --> 00:52:40.850
They make you swear and swear.

886
00:52:40.884 --> 00:52:43.685
<i>Defend the king. obey the king.</i>

887
00:52:43.720 --> 00:52:45.254
<i>obey your father.</i>

888
00:52:45.288 --> 00:52:48.557
protect the innocent.
defend the weak.

889
00:52:48.591 --> 00:52:52.427
But what if your father
despises the king?

890
00:52:52.461 --> 00:52:56.064
What if the king
massacres the innocent?

891
00:52:56.098 --> 00:52:58.300
It's too much.

892
00:52:58.334 --> 00:53:01.870
No matter what you do.
you're forsaking one vow or another.

893
00:53:01.904 --> 00:53:04.739
Where did you find this beast?

894
00:53:06.008 --> 00:53:08.977
She is a truer Knight
than you will ever be.

895
00:53:09.012 --> 00:53:11.313
Kingslayer.

896
00:53:11.347 --> 00:53:13.949
Kingslayer.

897
00:53:13.983 --> 00:53:16.284
What a king he was.

898
00:53:16.319 --> 00:53:19.989
<i>Here's to Aerys Targaryen.</i>
<i>the second of his name.</i>

899
00:53:20.023 --> 00:53:23.192
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.
Protector of the realm.

900
00:53:23.227 --> 00:53:27.197
and to the sword
I shoved in his back.

901
00:53:28.399 --> 00:53:31.434
You are a man without honor.

902
00:53:32.803 --> 00:53:34.938
Do you know

903
00:53:34.972 --> 00:53:38.208
I've never been with
any woman but Cersei?

904
00:53:38.242 --> 00:53:41.077
So in my own way.

905
00:53:41.079 --> 00:53:46.250
I have more honor
than poor old dead Ned.

906
00:53:47.886 --> 00:53:50.121
What was the name of that
bastard so in he fathered?

907
00:53:50.155 --> 00:53:53.759
- Brienne.
- No. that wasn't it.

908
00:53:53.793 --> 00:53:57.963
Snow. a bastard from the North.

909
00:53:57.998 --> 00:54:00.767
Now. when...
when good old Ned

910
00:54:00.801 --> 00:54:04.204
came home with
some whore's baby.

911
00:54:04.238 --> 00:54:07.407
did you pretend to love it?

912
00:54:07.441 --> 00:54:11.611
<i>No. You're not very good</i>
<i>at pretending.</i>

913
00:54:11.645 --> 00:54:13.813
<i>You're an honest woman.</i>

914
00:54:13.847 --> 00:54:17.216
You hated that boy. didn't you?

915
00:54:17.250 --> 00:54:19.685
<i>How could you not hate him?</i>

916
00:54:19.719 --> 00:54:22.320
<i>The walking. talking reminder</i>

917
00:54:22.388 --> 00:54:26.023
that the honorable
Lord Eddard Stark

918
00:54:26.058 --> 00:54:28.793
fucked another woman.

919
00:54:31.130 --> 00:54:33.431
Your sword.

920
00:54:37.804 --> 00:54:41.141
I told you what would happen.

921
00:54:41.175 --> 00:54:43.443
All of you...

922
00:54:45.080 --> 00:54:49.416
I told you what would happen
if you served me loyally...

923
00:54:49.451 --> 00:54:51.619
<i>and what would happen</i>
<i>if you did not.</i>

924
00:54:51.653 --> 00:54:54.488
What are you doing?
What have you done?

925
00:54:54.522 --> 00:54:56.723
If there's any who still question
whether your new lord

926
00:54:56.758 --> 00:54:58.392
means what he says...

927
00:55:01.029 --> 00:55:04.031
Here is the answer
to your question.

928
00:55:04.065 --> 00:55:07.234
<i>( Crowd gasps. murmurs )</i>

929
00:55:13.242 --> 00:55:15.577
No!

930
00:55:25.756 --> 00:55:28.925
<i>( Theme music playing )</i>

931
00:55:28.950 --> 00:55:32.950
== sync. corrected by <font color="#00ff00">elderman</font> ==
